# NN_MULTIPROCESSING_MAX_CHILD_TIME is deliberately ABSENT (trap #5).
# Writing it here, even as its own default of 1800, hands
# Pool::timeout(float) a string via Laravel's env(), which returns STRINGS,
# and every Forking multiprocessing runner dies with a TypeError.
# RULE for this whole file: never set a key unless the value must DIFFER
# from the PHP default in config/nntmux.php. Restating a default is not
# documentation, it is a type change.

